  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 354 AM CDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nThe remainder of the forecast continues to look seasonably cool\nand dry into the middle of next week. A broad high pressure \nsystem builds into the Midwest late Friday and then moves east \nthrough the Great Lakes Saturday. Another upper level short wave\nthen moves through the Midwest Saturday night into Sunday. This\npushes a reinforcing cold front through Missouri and Illinois \nlate Sunday which will lower temperatures again. The GFS is \nprinting out a few specks of QPF Sunday along the front, however\nmoisture return ahead will be minimal at best so I don't think \nthere will be much if any precip. Temperatures will be a little \nwarmer in the low to mid 70s on both Saturday and Sunday with \nfull or nearly full sunshine. Then temperatures drop into the \nmid 60s to around 70 again Monday and Tuesday behind the \nreinforcing front. The wind swings back around to the southwest \non Wednesday as the high moves over the East Coast and \ntemperatures rise back into the mid and upper 70s.",
